Planar (SB) Ewald long-range dispersion examples
====================================================

Planar Lennard-Jones liquid-vapor slab (1267 atoms, fully periodic) using the
smooth-damped planar dispersion long-range solvers:

  in.ewald_disp_planar   kspace_style ewald/disp/planar (1-D z Fourier sum)
  in.pppm_disp_planar    kspace_style pppm/disp/planar  (mesh-accelerated, O(N))

Both pair with the matched pair_style lj/disp/planar, which does the full LJ
to r_cut and fades the 1/r^6 dispersion out smoothly over [r_cut, r_cut+Delta].
The kspace style adds the smooth r>r_cut dispersion tail with a 1-D z Fourier
sum, and folds the real-space slab correction into its reciprocal coefficients
(no separate real-space correction step).  The thermo output includes the
long-range surface tension gamma = (Lz/2)(P_zz - (P_xx+P_yy)/2).

A Kokkos-accelerated pppm/disp/planar/kk variant runs the mesh solve on the device
(add "-k on t <N> -sf kk" and use kspace_style pppm/disp/planar/kk).

These styles require fully periodic boundaries and must NOT be combined with the
EW3DC "kspace_modify slab" correction.
